@startuml LMS_Arch_05_Pipe_Filter
title Architecture 5: Pipe-and-Filter (Circulation & Reminders)

skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

database "Active Loans\n[Data Store]" as DS_Loans #FCE4EC
database "Daily Returns\n[Data Store]" as DS_Returns #FCE4EC

rectangle "Read Issued Loans\n(Filter 1)" as F1 #E3F2FD
rectangle "Identify Returns\n(Filter 2)" as F2 #E3F2FD

rectangle "Identify Overdues & Status\n(Filter / Fork 3)" as F3 #FFF9C4

rectangle "Issue Return Receipts\n& Release Holds\n(Filter 4)" as F4 #E8F5E9
rectangle "Find Fines Due\n(Filter 5)" as F5 #E8F5E9

rectangle "Issue Overdue Reminder\n(Filter 6)" as F6 #FFE0B2

database "Receipts & Hold Notifications\n[Output]" as DS_Receipts #FCE4EC
database "Email Dispatch Queue\n[SMTP]" as DS_Mail #FCE4EC

DS_Loans ==> F1 : pipe [Active Loans]
DS_Returns ==> F2 : pipe [Returned Books]

F1 ==> F3 : pipe [Loan Records]
F2 ==> F3 : pipe [Return Records]

F3 ==> F4 : pipe [Normal Returns]
F3 ==> F5 : pipe [Overdue Records]

F4 ==> DS_Receipts : pipe [Receipts]
F5 ==> F6 : pipe [Fines Calculated]
F6 ==> DS_Mail : pipe [SMTP Packets]

note bottom of F6
  **Pipe-and-Filter Pattern:**
  Stateless filters for daily cron jobs:
  overdue calc, reminders, hold expiry.
end note

@enduml
